<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-14293] .NET: AffinityKey does not work</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-14293</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;tt&gt;AffinityKey&lt;/tt&gt; does not work as expected - &lt;tt&gt;Affinity&lt;/tt&gt; property is not used for affinity calculation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is caused by &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-13160&quot; title=&quot;.NET: wrong affinity key registration with AffinityKeyMapped attribute&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-13160&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-13160&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;: &lt;tt&gt;AffinityKey&lt;/tt&gt; system type is overwritten by &lt;tt&gt;UnmanagedCallbacks.BinaryTypeGet&lt;/tt&gt; call. As a result, this type becomes a regular, user type, and does not map to a corresponding type on the Java side.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Add test that combines QueryEntity with AffinityKey&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Check that other system types (IgniteUuid, etc) don&apos;t have this problem, add tests&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Make sure we never overwrite system types during registration&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Improve examples tests: Thick Sql example provides inconsistent output due to this bug&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
</description>
